-- title:
--   Complete splitting forces trivial ramification in the value group
-- statement:
--   Let $F'/F$ be an extension of fields with $F'$ finite-dimensional over $F$, let $\mathcal{O}$ be a valuation subring of $F$, and let $\iota$ be a finite index type equipped with a family $(\mathcal{O}'_i)_{i\in\iota}$ of valuation subrings of $F'$. Assume: the family is injective, i.e. distinct indices give distinct valuation subrings; each $\mathcal{O}'_i$ lies over $\mathcal{O}$, in the sense that the preimage of $\mathcal{O}'_i$ under the structure map $F \to F'$ is exactly $\mathcal{O}$; and the number of indices is at least the degree, $[F':F] \le |\iota|$. Then for every index $i$ and every nonzero $g \in F'$ there exists $h \in F$ such that the canonical valuation of $\mathcal{O}'_i$, with values in its value group, takes the value $1$ at $h g$ (the image of $h$ in $F'$ times $g$); equivalently, $hg$ is a unit of $\mathcal{O}'_i$. Thus every element of $F'^{\times}$ is, up to a factor from $F^{\times}$, a unit at $\mathcal{O}'_i$: the value group of $\mathcal{O}'_i$ is generated by the image of the value group of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   This is the value-group half of the classical corollary to the fundamental inequality $\sum_i e_i f_i \le [F':F]$ of valuation theory: if a valuation of $F$ admits at least $[F':F]$ distinct prolongations to $F'$, then each of them is unramified in the sense that its value group does not grow, $e = 1$. It holds for arbitrary fields and valuations of arbitrary rank, and is used in the construction of prolongations of regular local data on curves, via [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_prolongation_of_card_roots_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_prolongation_of_card_roots_eq).
